#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:164
msgid "`proxy` / `proxyConfig` / `basicAuth`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:166
msgid ""
"`proxy<'proxyValue>` selects which traffic each slot covers, parametric "
"on a single `'proxyValue` type that is either a plain URL `string` or a "
"full `proxyConfig` record:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:186
msgid ""
"`proxyConfig.noProxy` accepts the upstream comma-separated host pattern "
"syntax (`localhost`, `*.internal`, `192.168.0.0/16`, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:201
msgid ""
"`acceptInvalidCerts` skips SSL/TLS certificate verification; "
"`acceptInvalidHostnames` skips the cert's hostname check. Both default to"
" `false` — opt in only for self-signed certs in a development build, "
"internal staging, or mTLS experiments. **Do not enable either in shipped "
"production code.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:207
msgid "Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:209
msgid "DOM Web Fetch types are intentionally unbound"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:211
msgid ""
"The DOM `Request` / `Response` / `RequestInit` types live in "
"`@rescript/core`'s sparse Web Fetch surface, which doesn't cover the "
"streaming / progress / clone APIs the plugin exposes. Rather than ship a "
"partially-typed binding, `fetch` is left polymorphic and the call site "
"picks a strategy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:217
msgid ""
"**Type annotation** — when you already have a concrete record-or-object "
"type that captures the fields you touch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:226
msgid ""
"**`Obj.magic` + inline structural type** — the minimum-cost path, useful "
"when you only need a couple of fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:236
msgid ""
"**External binding** — for repeated access, wrap the surface you actually"
" use behind a `@send` / `@get` external block in your own module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:240
msgid ""
"A typed Web Fetch surface is deferred to a follow-up sub-steering (see "
"the package CHANGELOG)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:243
msgid "`proxy<'proxyValue>` takes a single type parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:245
msgid ""
"Because `proxy<'proxyValue>` has one type variable shared across the "
"`all` / `http` / `https` slots, mixing a `string` URL in one slot with a "
"full `proxyConfig` record in another is a type error when you build the "
"record with the `~init` ReScript record syntax. Two workarounds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:251
msgid ""
"**Unify the type**: wrap every slot in `proxyConfig`, even when you only "
"need a URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:253
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Use a JS object literal**: object literals don't enforce the type "
"parameter, so a mixed `{\"http\": \"http://...\", \"https\": {\"url\": "
"\"https://...\", \"basicAuth\": …}}` shape is accepted as `'init`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:258
msgid "`dangerousSettings` ships disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-http.md:260
msgid ""
"If you omit `danger` from `init`, both checks stay on by default. The "
"plugin's Tauri-level capability layer cannot re-enable them — only an "
"explicit `init.danger` record can. This keeps secure-by-default behaviour"
" visible at the call site."
msgstr ""

